I don't see why .xorxes. is being asked to explain himself. Translation is
not an easy task, especially with works of art.

The rules for written Lojban are extremely loose and very simple. Regarding
specifically your issue with capitalization, Lojban /doesn't care/ about it
except for marking non-penultimate stress; {krefu}, {KREfu}, {KREFU}, etc.
are the same word. Using capitalization for visual purposes that do not
affect the meaning of the text grammatically or semantically are not
"clearly against the rules" for the simple reason that the rules don't have
anything to say on the matter, and they shouldn't. Further, with the recent
in comparison to the writing of la.alis. use of accents instead of capitals
to mark non-standard stress, the case of lerfu is made nearly irrelevant
where jbogerna is concerned.

.xorxes. was and is well within his artistic license in making la.alis.. If
you have disagreements as to his artistic choices, you're more than welcome
to make your own translation.


